“Decorating a piece of time” gets at what I like about the AI-nime idea. The frame can be rough and the timing can be exact. In the peach scene, one extra beat before she puts the slice down can turn a cute moment into a gut punch. Put the thunder there and it’s melodrama. Hold it until after the cut and the audience sits with her for a second before the world comes crashing back in.

That’s where the Pantheon ideas become things we can play. Reality is the peach on the table. Meaning is the memory tucked inside an ordinary gesture. Interface is how we let the audience find it. Show her face first and we inherit her suspicion. Show his hands first and we might feel the tenderness before we know what it costs her. Same footage, same two people. A different fifteen seconds to live through.